# Line endings, decided here rather than by whoever cloned.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to CRLF on
# checkout. A `.sh` that goes through that conversion is no longer executable on
# Linux: the shebang reads `bash\r`, and the loader reports
# `/usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory` - which names an
# interpreter that does not exist rather than the file that was converted.
#
# That is not a Windows-only problem. It hits any WSL, container or CI run that
# shares a Windows checkout, and the extension is installed by copying this
# repository into a project, so a converted script travels with it.
#
# So: every text file in this repository is checked out with LF, on every
# platform. `.editorconfig` already asks editors for the same thing; this is the
# half git enforces.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for the two that break loudly, so the intent survives an edit
# to the line above.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
